Changelog
=========

Notable changes to the MD/hv-config content and tooling in this repo. Newest
first. Cosmetic tweaks to docs/index.html (wording, formatting) are omitted; see
git log for those.

The blobs in bin/ are built output, committed deliberately (they are the evidence
the boot matrix and md-artefacts cite). "byte-identical" below always means
verified with scripts/verify.sh, which rebuilds each config and compares.


2026-08-12
----------

Added

  - patches/_test/README -- what the experimental tree is worth, as opposed to
    what each config in it changes. Two things it exists to state plainly. The
    new-format configs (hvmd_v1, hvmd_v1_pciex) need an entirely different set
    of binaries from everything else here: a hypervisor and reset vector built
    by us from the OpenSPARC *T2* release sources, a T2-release OBP image, and
    a QEMU carrying the hv-private console UART -- nothing in fw_blobs/ can run
    them, and the T2-generation hv likewise rejects the old-format configs. And
    none of the new-format work is verified on a Solaris boot as committed: the
    effort since 2026-08-04 went into describing and enumerating hardware, not
    into re-testing the boot after each step.

  - _test/hvmd_v1 -- the hv MD in the format the T2-generation hypervisor
    requires (content-version 1.0, two-level: an hv MD of container nodes plus
    a guest MD found through mdpa), with LDC endpoints modelled on Sun's own
    single-guest Legion pair. The guest MD gains forward arcs under
    virtual-devices (arcs are directional; without them every device is "not
    found"), compatible as a list everywhere, an openboot/variables subtree,
    and a console compatible list ordered "qcn" first, which is what makes
    console input work.

  - _test/hvmd_v1_pciex -- hvmd_v1 plus a PCIe root complex, guest side and hv
    side, copied from Sun's 1c1t descriptors. Deliberately kept separate: it
    provokes an error path rather than booting. Its result is negative and
    useful -- the hypervisor answers EINVAL and describing a bus to it changes
    nothing, so the bus cannot be served that way.

  - scripts/mdcompare.py -- compares two binary MDs property by property, so a
    config can be checked against a reference (or against the exact blob that
    last booted) instead of reasoned about on its own.

Changed

  - perfctraccess = 0 on the guest node in the new-format configs, matching
    Sun's Legion configuration. Non-zero lets the perf-register hypercalls
    reach physical addresses no emulator maps, faulting inside the hypervisor;
    a guest triggers it with `kstat -p dram:::`. The old-format configs keep 1
    on purpose -- see patches/_test/README for why, and why that is not an
    oversight in either direction.


2026-07-23
----------

Added

  - scripts/verify.sh -- rebuilds every config into a temp directory and compares
    against what is committed, catching source/blob drift (edit a .pdesc, forget
    to make, commit -- git shows a changed source next to an unchanged blob and
    says nothing). Also re-checks the OpenSPARC_T1_rebuild byte-identity proof
    against bin/_reference/, flags stray files in a config dir, and exits 2 (not
    0) when it cannot run at all. Safe to run any time; writes nothing under
    bin/.

Changed

  - Firmware is now passed as a second -L, not symlinked into each config. Every
    bin/<config>/ had carried openboot.bin, q.bin, reset.bin and nvram1 (and an
    unused netcons) as symlinks into fw_blobs/. The links were absolute
    (/git/md/fw_blobs/...), so all 55 dangled in any clone outside /git/md -- no
    config worked out of the box for anyone but the author. They were also
    unnecessary: QEMU's -L may be repeated and is searched in order (commit
    4524051c32, added in 2013 precisely "so you don't have to create a symlink
    farm for all the rom blobs"). A config dir now holds only its built blobs;
    invoke with "-L <config> -L fw_blobs". The fw-blobs machinery is gone from
    every Makefile.

    First-match-wins caveat: a directory carrying its own copy of a blob shadows
    every -L after it -- check with "-L help" or "-trace load_file".

  - OpenSPARC_T1_rebuild now builds all three configs Sun shipped -- 1up, 1g2p,
    1g32p -- instead of 1up alone, matching the CONFIGS list in Sun's own
    niagara/Makefile. 1up is a single-strand, single-guest machine and on its own
    exercised only a fraction of mdgen; 1g32p-md.bin is 9104 bytes to 1up's 2408.
    All six blobs rebuild byte-identical to Sun's originals, widening the
    toolchain-fidelity proof from one config to three. verify.sh's drift and
    stray-file checks were generalised off a hardcoded 1up-* list at the same
    time.

  - Makefile usage-comment paths for fw_blobs made relative (they had named the
    author-only absolute /git/md/fw_blobs).


Earlier
-------

The founding content: Sun's unmodified 2006 sources under
bin/_reference/OpenSPARC_T1_original/, the OpenSPARC_T1_rebuild byte-identity
proof, and the boot-fix patch chain -- t1_boot_fix (memory/cpus/cache nodes plus
mmu-page-size-list and mmu-#va-bits platform props, the live-kmdb-proven-minimal
set for a clean sun4v boot on illumos/OpenSolaris snv_134) and tlb_fix (adds a
per-cpu tlb node). See patches/ for the reviewable diffs and docs/index.html for
the boot matrix.
